.TH OTSDAQ-MU2E-TOOLS 7 "2026-10-06" "otsdaq-mu2e 11.03.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
otsdaq-mu2e-tools \- index of the scripts, Tcl files and configuration
fragments in otsdaq-mu2e/tools
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I otsdaq\-mu2e/tools
holds 52 files besides
.IR CMakeLists.txt .
They cover FPGA programming, PCIe reset, installation and bootstrap,
configuration snapshots, and test-stand utilities.
This page gives one line per file, from a reading of each.
Files with their own page are marked (1).
.PP
How the files are installed:
.IP \(bu 2
The top-level
.I CMakeLists.txt
copies the whole directory into the build tree and installs it
.RB ( "INSTALL(DIRECTORY tools ...)" ).
Only four scripts are registered with
.B cet_script
and so placed on the
.B PATH
of a built area:
.BR create_mu2e_ots_snapshot.sh ,
.BR reset_mu2e_ots_snapshot.sh ,
.B create_mu2e_ops_snapshot.sh
and
.BR reset_mu2e_ops_snapshot.sh .
.IP \(bu 2
On the DAQ nodes, the shifter procedure runs the firmware scripts from
.IR /home/mu2ehwdev .
The
.I program_all
and
.I program_flash_all
scripts call
.I /home/mu2ehwdev/program_one_FPGA_AL9.sh
and
.I /home/mu2ehwdev/program_flash_one_FPGA_AL9.sh
by absolute path.
This repository does not record whether those copies are symbolic links into
a checkout or independent copies.
.PP
The
.B _AL9
scripts are the AlmaLinux 9 generation.
The unsuffixed
.I *.sh
variants with the same names are the earlier SL7-era versions.
They
.B source
.I reset_PCIe.sh
into the caller's shell instead of running
.B sudo reset_PCIe_AL9.sh
as a child.
.SS FPGA programming and PCIe reset (AL9, current)
.TP
.BR program_all_FPGA_AL9.sh (1)
Load one
.I .bit
into every JTAG-attached FPGA, then
.B sudo reset_PCIe_AL9.sh
by default.
.TP
.BR program_flash_all_FPGA_AL9.sh (1)
Erase, write and verify one
.I .mcs
in every FPGA's BPI flash, boot from it, then reset PCIe.
.TP
.BR boot_from_flash_all_DTCs_AL9.sh (1)
Make every JTAG-attached FPGA reload its flash image, then reset PCIe.
.TP
.BR reset_PCIe_AL9.sh (1)
Kill device users, unload
.BR mu2e ,
remove and rescan the Xilinx 7042/7043 devices, reload, and print register
0x9004.
.TP
.B reset_PCIe_AL9_sudowrapper.sh
Three lines: runs
.B sudo
on the
.I ~mu2ehwdev/ots_spack/srcs/otsdaq\-mu2e/tools
copy of
.IR reset_PCIe_AL9.sh .
It is meant to be installed as
.IR ~mu2ehwdev/reset_PCIe_AL9.sh .
.TP
.B program_one_FPGA_AL9.sh
.RB [ NORESET ]
.I N bitfile
\(em program JTAG target
.IR N .
Takes
.IR /tmp/mu2e.lock ,
works in
.IR /home/mu2ehwdev ,
and logs to
.IR .Xil/vivado_user_log.txt .
.TP
.B program_flash_one_FPGA_AL9.sh
.I N mcsfile
.RI [ flashpart ]
\(em write flash on target
.I N
(default part
.BR mt28gu01gaax1e\-bpi\-x16 ).
No lock and no
.B #!
line.
.TP
.B program_both_DTCs_AL9.sh
.I bit0
.RI [ bit1 ]
\(em program targets 0 and 1, then
.BR "sudo reset_PCIe_AL9.sh" .
Takes the lock.
.TP
.B program_flash_both_DTCs_AL9.sh
.I mcs
.RI [ part0 " [" part1 ]]
or
.I mcs0 part0 mcs1 part1
\(em write the flash of targets 0 and 1.
No reset.
.TP
.B boot_from_flash_both_DTCs_AL9.sh
Boot targets 0 and 1 from flash, then
.BR "sudo reset_PCIe_AL9.sh" .
Takes the lock.
If the lock is held, it sends SIGTERM to any running mu2edaq-operations
.I read_dtc_temps.sh
and proceeds once that has gone.
.TP
.B reset_both_JAs_AL9.sh
Run
.I /home/mu2eshift/JA_ots_setup.sh
as
.B mu2eshift
on this host over
.BR ssh ,
to set up both jitter attenuators.
.TP
.B setup_vivado_lab_AL9.sh
Source Vivado Lab 2021.2.
Kills every
.BR vivado_lab ,
.B java
and
.B hw_server
process the user may signal, deletes
.I ~/.Xilinx
and
.IR /tmp/.Xilinx ,
then runs
.I clear_vivado_lab.tcl
twice.
.TP
.B find_JTAG_usb_AL9.sh
List the USB JTAG adapters by vendor:product, and print the sysfs
unbind/bind commands that reset one.
.SS FPGA programming and PCIe reset (legacy, SL7 era)
.TP
.B program_one_FPGA.sh
.I N bitfile
\(em program target
.IR N ,
then
.B source reset_PCIe.sh .
.TP
.B program_both_DTCs.sh
.I bit0
.RI [ bit1 ]
\(em program targets 0 and 1, then
.B source reset_PCIe.sh .
.TP
.B program_flash_one_FPGA.sh
.I N mcs
.RI [ part ]
\(em write flash on target
.IR N ,
then
.B source reset_PCIe.sh .
.TP
.B program_flash_both_DTCs.sh
Write flash on targets 0 and 1, then
.B source reset_PCIe.sh .
.TP
.B boot_from_flash_both_DTCs.sh
Boot targets 0 and 1 from flash, then
.B source reset_PCIe.sh .
.TP
.B erase_flash_both_DTCs.sh
.RI [ part0 " [" part1 ]]
\(em erase the configuration flash of targets 0 and 1, then
.B source reset_PCIe.sh .
.TP
.B reset_PCIe.sh
SL7 predecessor of
.IR reset_PCIe_AL9.sh .
It sends one
.B kill
(SIGTERM) to device holders and
.B killall \-9 xdaq.exe ,
makes one
.B rmmod
attempt (exit 1 on failure), then removes, rescans and reloads.
It sources
.IR /root/setup_pcie.sh .
.SS Vivado Tcl (run by the scripts above with vivado_lab \-mode batch)
.TP
.B program_one_FPGA.tcl
Program device 0 of target
.I argv[0]
with
.IR argv[1] .
.TP
.B program_both_DTCs.tcl
Program device 0 of targets 0 and 1.
.TP
.B program_flash_one_FPGA.tcl
Create the cfgmem object for part
.IR argv[2] ,
erase, program and verify the flash with
.IR argv[1] ,
then
.BR boot_hw_device .
.TP
.B program_flash_both_DTCs.tcl
The same for targets 0 and 1.
.TP
.B erase_flash_both_DTCs.tcl
Erase the configuration flash of targets 0 and 1.
.TP
.B boot_from_flash_one_DTC.tcl
.B boot_hw_device
on device 0 of target
.IR argv[0] .
.TP
.B boot_from_flash_both_DTCs.tcl
.B boot_hw_device
on targets 0 and 1.
.TP
.B clear_vivado_lab.tcl
Open and close the hardware server and target twice, to clear a stuck
session.
.SS Firmware and source checks
.TP
.BR check_firmware_version.sh (1)
Compare register 0x9004 of devices 0 and 1 with an expected value.
Exit 0 on mismatch.
.TP
.BR check_status.sh (1)
.BR "git fetch" / status / "remote \-v"
over eleven MRB-era underscore-named source directories.
This is not a hardware check.
.SS Installation and bootstrap
.TP
.B install_ots_ops.sh
.I target_dir
\(em create an operations workspace.
It clones
.IR otsdaq\-mu2e\-config ,
links
.IR setup_ots.sh ,
copies
.I db_setup_ots.sh
and
.I mongodb_setup.sh
from
.IR ~/.secrets ,
downloads
.I mu2e\-quick\-spack\-start_v0.28.sh
from the
.B develop
branch on GitHub and runs it, then runs
.B UpdateOTS.sh \-\-tables
for eight subsystems.
.TP
.B mu2e\-quick\-spack\-start.sh
Symbolic link to
.IR mu2e\-quick\-spack\-start_v0.28.sh .
.TP
.B mu2e\-quick\-spack\-start_v0.28.sh
Spack bootstrap of the Mu2e TDAQ software stack into an empty directory.
It uses
.I /mu2e/spack_v0.28
and cvmfs upstreams.
Open issue #245 covers its fetch of a file that no longer exists.
.TP
.B mu2e\-quick\-spack\-start_v1.1.sh
The same against the Spack v1.1 upstreams.
It has no
.B \-\-no\-emacs
option.
.TP
.B quick\-mrb\-start.sh
MRB/UPS-era download of
.I otsdaq_demo
(Eric Flumerfelt, 2016).
.TP
.B quick_mu2e_ots_install.sh
MRB-era installer, sourced as root.
It installs packages with
.B yum
and fetches from
.I otsdaq.fnal.gov
and cdcvs Redmine URLs.
.TP
.B quick_mu2e_trigger_ots_install.sh
The same for the trigger area.
.TP
.B build\-mu2e_tdaq.sh
CI-style build of the bundle, driven by
.BR WORKSPACE ,
.BR QUAL ,
.B BUILDTYPE
and
.BR COPYBACK_DEPS .
.TP
.B mu2e_tdaq_software\-cfg\-1.00.00
UPS
.B buildFW
bundle configuration, pinning otsdaq 2.06.11, mu2e_pcie_utils v2_08_05 and
otsdaq_mu2e v1_03_02, among others.
.SS Configuration snapshots
These are the four scripts placed on the
.BR PATH .
Each takes
.BI \-\-name " snapshot"
and requires that the user is in the
.B mu2eshift
k5login.
.TP
.B create_mu2e_ots_snapshot.sh
Zip a
.I Data
and a
.I databases
area (given by
.BR \-\-data ,
.BR \-\-database )
and copy them with
.B scp
to
.I /mu2e/DataFiles/UserSnapshots/
as
.BR mu2eshift .
.TP
.B create_mu2e_ops_snapshot.sh
The same for the operations area (all Data and databases folders).
.TP
.B reset_mu2e_ots_snapshot.sh
Replace the local configuration with a named snapshot.
It downloads
.I get_mu2e_snapshot_data.sh
and
.I get_mu2e_snapshot_database.sh
from the
.B develop
branch on GitHub
.RB ( "wget \-\-no\-check\-certificate" )
and runs them.
.B \-\-list
runs
.B ls
on
.I /mu2e/DataFiles/UserSnapshots/
through
.BR mu2eshift@mu2egateway01 .
.TP
.B reset_mu2e_ops_snapshot.sh
The same for the operations area.
.TP
.B get_mu2e_snapshot_data.sh
Fetch and unpack
.IR snapshot_ NAME _Data.zip
into
.BR $USER_DATA .
It deletes
.IR Logs ,
.IR ARTDAQConfigurations ,
.I TriggerConfigurations
and
.I OutputData
there.
.TP
.B get_mu2e_snapshot_database.sh
Fetch and unpack
.I snapshot_ NAME _database.zip
into the filesystem database named by
.BR ARTDAQ_DATABASE_URI ,
keeping a
.I .bak
of the previous one.
.SS Logbook
.TP
.B post_to_ecl.sh
.I title message
\(em run
.I /home/mu2eshift/ecl_post.sh
as
.B mu2eshift
on this host over
.BR ssh .
.SS Test-stand and demo utilities
.TP
.B start_collection.sh
.B ssh
to mu2edaq05, 06, 14, 17 and 16 (hard-coded) and run
.I ~/test_stand/ots/collect.sh
on each in parallel.
.TP
.B collect.sh
For 16 minutes, sample DTC register 0x93C8 (cleared first) once a second
into
.IR ~/otsdaq_ HOST _lock.txt .
.TP
.B generate_plotscript.sh
Write a gnuplot script,
.IR script.p ,
that plots the
.I collect.sh
files for the 10-DTC chain.
.TP
.B distributed_setup_ots.sh
.I subsystem
\(em source
.IB /home/ base /ots/setup_ots.sh
for
.BR hwdev ,
.B sync
or
.BR stm .
.TP
.B sync_demo_ots.sh
Start ots for the sync demo.
On mu2edaq06 it also starts it on mu2edaq04 and mu2edaq05 over
.BR ssh .
.SS Configuration fragments
.TP
.B MacroMakerModeFhiclDump_edit.fcl
Example MacroMaker-mode FHiCL for two DTCs with hardware-emulated ROCs:
.B DTCFrontEndInterface
with
.BR ROCDTCHardwareEmulated .
.PP
The legacy, MRB-era and test-stand files carry 2016\(en2023 hostnames and
paths.
They are listed here for completeness and are not part of the current
shifter procedure.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /tmp/mu2e.lock
PID symbolic-link lock, shared by the
.B _AL9
programming and reset scripts and by mu2edaq-operations
.IR read_dtc_temps.sh .
.TP
.I /home/xilinx/Vivado_Lab/2021.2/settings64.sh
Vivado Lab environment sourced by every FPGA script.
.TP
.I /home/mu2ehwdev/.Xil/vivado_user_log.txt
Audit line per FPGA load or flash write.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR program_all_FPGA_AL9.sh (1),
.BR reset_PCIe_AL9.sh (1),
.BR program_flash_all_FPGA_AL9.sh (1),
.BR boot_from_flash_all_DTCs_AL9.sh (1),
.BR check_firmware_version.sh (1),
.BR check_status.sh (1)
.PP
.I otsdaq\-mu2e/doc/INTERFACES.md
covers the plugins and the run-control interfaces.
.SH AUTHOR
Written for the September 2026 DAQ mega-review from the files at
.I otsdaq-mu2e
commit 828cfe24.
The scripts are by the Mu2e TDAQ group, chiefly Ryan Rivera.
